# MidSphere Autonomous Agent Rules & Operational Standards
# Version: 2.0.0 (universalized)
# Authority: root AGENTS.md · ARCHITECTURE.md · DESIGN.md

===============================================================================
SECTION 0: DOCUMENT AUTHORITY
===============================================================================

0.1 Before writing code, agents MUST read in order:
    1. ARCHITECTURE.md
    2. DESIGN.md
    3. AGENTS.md
    4. This file (.agents/rules)

0.2 resource/ and datahub-agent-hackathon.md are reference material.
    Do not delete or rewrite them as part of MidSphere implementation.

0.3 Antigravity SDK patterns: .agents/sdk.md

===============================================================================
SECTION 1: SYSTEM PHILOSOPHY
===============================================================================

1.1 CONTEXT MANDATE
DataHub's context graph is the system of record. Prefer MCP reads over invented schemas.

1.2 CLOSED-LOOP WRITE-BACK
When mutations are enabled, findings write back:
  - Tags: QUARANTINED, CIRCUIT_BROKEN, MIDSPHERE_AUDIT
  - Structured properties: midsphere.gate_status, risk_score, job_id, pr_url
  - MBOM via save_document + related_assets
  - Optional Cloud-only GraphQL raiseIncident (never required for OSS)

1.3 NO ENFORCEMENT FICTION
Forbidden: claiming MCP auto-blocks all consumers of quarantined entities.
Allowed: advisory metadata + MidSphere Consumer Gate.

1.4 NON-DESTRUCTIVE
Quarantines are reversible. No DROP/DELETE warehouse data. No hard-delete of catalog entities.

===============================================================================
SECTION 2: REAL MCP TOOL NAMES ONLY
===============================================================================

2.1 READ
  search, get_entities, list_schema_fields, get_lineage,
  get_lineage_paths_between, get_dataset_queries, search_documents

2.2 WRITE (TOOLS_IS_MUTATION_ENABLED=true)
  add_tags, remove_tags, add_structured_properties,
  remove_structured_properties, save_document, update_description

2.3 FORBIDDEN / NONEXISTENT
  datahub_get_lineage, datahub_add_tag, datahub_create_incident,
  create_incident as an MCP tool

